      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T17:20:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not familiar enough with ztest, but can these sleeps be avoided, so we don\u0027t slow down the overall test time?\n\nIs there a way to fake the `ktimer` used by `board_override_fan_control_duty()`?",
      "revId": "c2ed0cbb30f294248592d0dd771802382774da09",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec269e6a_44a558eb",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/skyrim/tests/winterhold/src/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T20:08:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The sleeps in ztest don\u0027t actually take that real clock time, they just speed along the emulated system such that we give tasks what would be 1 second of run time (ex. so several HOOK_TICK iterations can run before our test code resumes)",
      "parentUuid": "02a13ea9_d369c7fb",
      "revId": "c2ed0cbb30f294248592d0dd771802382774da09",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
